|~ What is declared under `::set`: the refusal of its constructor, and
   the verbs of sets, each with the parts of its object and its answer.
   A set is the vector in the one order
   without duplicates: a verb that keeps its subject's kind answers a
   set through the constructor of `::set`, and one that imposes an order
   answers the vector. ~|

:set/PayloadNotVecError
  |~~ `::set` builds a set from a vector, `::set[3 1 3]`; a payload of
      another kind is refused.

      ~(
        ::set{:not :a-vec}
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::set/PayloadNotVecError ::map]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:set/count
  |~~ The number of elements.

      ~(#[:a :b] | count | eq 2)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/count/size |~~ How many elements the set holds. ~~|
  ::number

:set/empty
  |~~ Whether the set holds no element.

      ~(#[] | empty | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/empty/vacant |~~ Whether the set holds no element. ~~|
  ::boolean

:set/first
  |~~ The least element, or null for the empty set.

      ~(#[:c :a :b] | first | eq :a)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/last
  |~~ The greatest element, or null for the empty set.

      ~(#[:c :a :b] | last | eq :c)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/sum
  |~~ The sum of the elements, each a number.

      ~(#[1 2 3] | sum | eq 6)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/sum/total |~~ The sum of the elements. ~~|
  ::number

:set/avg
  |~~ The mean of the elements, each a number, or null when there is none.

      ~(#[1 2 6] | avg | eq 3)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/avg/mean |~~ The mean of the elements, null for an empty set. ~~|
  #[::number ::null]

:set/min
  |~~ The least element, or the one whose key answers the least value.

      ~(#[3 1 4] | min | eq 1)
      ~(#[3 1 4] | min ~(desc) | eq 4)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/min/key |~~ The key the call gives, null when it gives none. ::holds~(is ::quote ::null) ~~| ~(at 0)

:set/max
  |~~ The greatest element, or the one whose key answers the greatest
      value.

      ~(#[3 1 4] | max | eq 4)
      ~(#[3 1 4] | max ~(desc) | eq 1)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/max/key |~~ The key the call gives, null when it gives none. ::holds~(is ::quote ::null) ~~| ~(at 0)

:set/filter
  |~~ The set of the elements whose predicate answers true.

      ~(#[1 2 3 4 5] | filter ~(gt 2) | eq #[3 4 5])
      ~(#[1 -2 3] | filter ::verb~(gt 0) | eq #[1 3])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/filter/predicate |~~ The code each element is run through, which answers a boolean. ::holds~(is ::quote) ~~| ~(/0)

:set/filter/kept |~~ The elements the predicate accepted. ~~|
  ::set

:set/every
  |~~ Whether the predicate answers true for every element.

      ~(#[2 4] | every ~(gt 0) | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/every/predicate |~~ The code each element is run through, which answers a boolean. ::holds~(is ::quote) ~~| ~(/0)

:set/every/all |~~ Whether the predicate held for every element. ~~|
  ::boolean

:set/any
  |~~ Whether the predicate answers true for some element.

      ~(#[1 2 3] | any ~(gt 2) | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/any/predicate |~~ The code each element is run through, which answers a boolean. ::holds~(is ::quote) ~~| ~(/0)

:set/any/some |~~ Whether the predicate held for some element. ~~|
  ::boolean

:set/groupBy
  |~~ The map of sets the key sorts the elements into.

      ~(#[1 2 3] | groupBy ~(if (gt 1) ~(:big) ~(:small)) | /big | eq #[2 3])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/groupBy/key |~~ The key the call gives, null when it gives none. ::holds~(is ::quote ::null) ~~| ~(at 0)

:set/groupBy/groups |~~ The elements filed under the keyword their key answered, each bucket a set. ~~|
  ::map

:set/indexBy
  |~~ The map of the elements under the key each answers, or under
      itself without a key.

      ~(#[{:id :a}] | indexBy ~(/id) | /a | eq {:id :a})
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/indexBy/key |~~ The key the call gives, null when it gives none. ::holds~(is ::quote ::null) ~~| ~(at 0)

:set/indexBy/index |~~ Each element under the keyword its key answered, the last of alike ones. ~~|
  ::map

:set/sort
  |~~ The vector of the elements in the one order, or by the value the
      key answers for each; the order is imposed, so the answer is the
      vector.

      ~(#[:y :x :z] | sort | eq [:x :y :z])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/sort/key |~~ The key the call gives, null when it gives none. ::holds~(is ::quote ::null) ~~| ~(at 0)

:set/sort/sorted |~~ The elements in the order the key ranks them, a vector. ~~|
  ::vec

:set/take
  |~~ The set of the least count elements.

      ~(#[:d :c :b :a] | take 2 | eq #[:a :b])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/take/count |~~ How many. ::holds~(is ::number) ~~| ~(/0)

:set/take/taken |~~ The least elements. ~~|
  ::set

:set/drop
  |~~ The set of the elements after the least count.

      ~(#[:d :c :b :a] | drop 2 | eq #[:c :d])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/drop/count |~~ How many. ::holds~(is ::number) ~~| ~(/0)

:set/drop/rest |~~ The elements after the least ones dropped. ~~|
  ::set

:set/at
  |~~ The element at the index in the one order, a negative one
      counting from the end, or null past either end.

      ~(#[:a :b :c] | at -1 | eq :c)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/at/default |~~ The value answered for a place the subject does not hold, null when it gives none. ~~| ~(at 1)

:set/at/index |~~ The index, a negative one counting from the end. ::holds~(is ::number) ~~| ~(/0)

:set/distinct
  |~~ The set itself.

      ~(#[1 2 3] | distinct | eq #[1 2 3])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/distinct/unique |~~ The set itself. ~~|
  ::set

:set/reverse
  |~~ The vector of the elements in the reverse of the one order.

      ~(#[:a :b :c] | reverse | eq [:c :b :a])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/reverse/reversed |~~ The elements from the greatest down, a vector. ~~|
  ::vec

:set/flat
  |~~ The set of the elements with one level of nesting spliced in, so
      a set of sets flattens into their union.

      ~(#[#[1 2] #[2 3]] | flat | eq #[1 2 3])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/flat/flattened |~~ The elements with the sets among them spliced in. ~~|
  ::set

:set/reduce
  |~~ The seed folded over the elements in the one order by the reducer.

      ~(#[1 2 3] | reduce 0 ~(add) | eq 6)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/reduce/reducer |~~ The code that folds an element into the value so far. ::holds~(is ::quote) ~~| ~(/1)

:set/reduce/seed |~~ The value the fold starts from. ~~| ~(/0)

:set/union
  |~~ The set of the elements of either set, merged in the one order;
      left without the other set, the union of the sets the set holds.

      ~(#[:a :b] | union #[:b :c] | eq #[:a :b :c])
      ~(#[#[1] #[2]] | union | eq #[1 2])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/union/with
  |~~ The value the subject is joined with, null when it gives none. ::holds~(is ::set ::null) ~~|
  ~(at 0)

:set/union/merged |~~ The elements of both sets. ~~|
  ::set

:set/minus
  |~~ The set of the elements the other set lacks.

      ~(#[:a :b :c] | minus #[:b] | eq #[:a :c])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/minus/with
  |~~ The value the subject is joined with, null when it gives none. ::holds~(is ::set ::null) ~~|
  ~(at 0)

:set/minus/remaining |~~ The elements the other set does not hold. ~~|
  ::set

:set/inter
  |~~ The set of the elements both sets hold.

      ~(#[:a :b :c] | inter #[:b :d] | eq #[:b])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/inter/with
  |~~ The value the subject is joined with, null when it gives none. ::holds~(is ::set ::null) ~~|
  ~(at 0)

:set/inter/common |~~ The elements both sets hold. ~~|
  ::set

:set/has
  |~~ Whether the set holds the element, found by a binary search in
      the one order.

      ~(#[:a :b :c] | has :b | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/has/element |~~ The element the call gives. ~~| ~(/0)

:set/has/held |~~ Whether the set holds the element. ~~|
  ::boolean

:set/contains
  |~~ Whether the set holds the element, the membership `has` asks,
      under the word a string answers for its substrings.

      ~(#[:a :b :c] | contains :b | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:set/contains/element |~~ The element the call gives. ~~| ~(/0)

:set/contains/found |~~ Whether the set holds the element. ~~|
  ::boolean
